                        "notes": "Patch release: two fixes found while reviewing 4.1.0 and measuring the demo.\n\n### 🐛 Bug Fixes\n- **A fenced code block inside a list item no longer grows a stray empty code block after the list.** The fence scanner accepted an opener behind a list marker but rejected its closer once the item's content indent reached four spaces — every nested bullet and every numbered step from `10.` up — so the fence looked open forever and the completer appended a second closer, on complete content too. Closers are now measured against the opener's depth, and the completer emits its own closer at that depth. ",
                        "notes_truncated": true,
                        "url": "https://github.com/beynar/svelte-streamdown/releases/tag/4.1.1"
